# Plan a larger change as a staged epic

Run this when a change is **too large for one issue**: it drafts a staged plan — `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ epics_folder }}/epic<N>_plan.md` — dividing the work into sequential stages of manageable issue specs that each flow through the normal lifecycle. A confirmed plan is then turned into real GitHub issues with the separate **`publish`** action.

**Drafting writes nothing on GitHub.** Only `/iflow-epic <N> publish [stage <k>]` creates issues, and only behind one consolidated confirm.

